From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: serialize and qualify exact Uke charger replies

Correlate owner/type/opcode/property/length under an IRQ-safe state lock, then
commit the response in the serialized request context. Enable notifications
through the same mutex without inventing undocumented ACK payload semantics.
Return negative firmware failures, reject sentinel data and signed overflows,
and expose read-only event generations without calling them firmware attach IDs.

Timeout and interrupted delivery have no wire transaction ID to disambiguate a
late reply. Keep that instance unavailable instead of replaying an uncertain
SET. PDR up or resume alone cannot prove a drain boundary. Preserve the bounded
SDP admission and keep every Uke battery setter blocked. No electrical profile,
port owner, OEM protection or firmware/calibration data is changed.

Direct protocol evidence: MiCode uke-v-oss
5712080a4b0c0b1a879e6d145c601c649ddaddfd, qti_battery_charger.c;
shared framework: upstream qcom_battmgr.c and pmic_glink.c (GPL-2.0-only).
Source candidate only; tests and builds deliberately deferred by the user.

